# Corpus rules for the graphify knowledge graph.
#
# The graph is the agent's first stop for any question about this codebase, so
# what it holds has to be worth answering from. Finished working output from a
# past agent run does not qualify: it is a snapshot of a codebase that has since
# moved, it is never revised, and because it is the only place in the corpus
# written partly in Russian, a Russian question lands in it by accident instead
# of in the code it is asking about.
#
# Agent-plugin sources, workspace state, and harness-specific directories are
# not product architecture. Keep them out of the graph explicitly;
# do not rely on the walker's dot-directory behaviour.
.workspace/
.djts/
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.tools/graphify/

# Guard against an accidental root-level Firecrawl cache. Research output belongs
# under .workspace/tools/firecrawl/, already excluded with the workspace.
.firecrawl/

# Code-only graph. The documentation site is no longer maintained.
docs/dj-track-similarity/

# Documents and media are outside the code corpus.
*.md
*.mdx
*.qmd
*.rst
*.skill
*.txt
*.html
*.yaml
*.yml
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.gdoc
*.gsheet
*.gslides
*.gif
*.jpeg
*.jpg
*.png
*.svg
*.webp
*.avi
*.m4a
*.m4v
*.mkv
*.mov
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.ogg
*.wav
*.webm

# Tests are outside the graph. With them in, they were 27% of the nodes and 30%
# of the edges, seeded queries with generic helpers (job(), _library(), profile())
# and made 88 of 254 communities test-dominated. Test files follow naming
# conventions (tests/test_<module>.py, *.test.mjs), so rg/Glob locates them
# without the graph.
tests/
*.test.mjs
